    halves:[["Scout finally recognizes the pale figure","in the corner of her room as Boo Radley."],["Atticus initially insists","that the full truth about Bob Ewell's death must be told."],["Sheriff Tate remains adamant","that the official account will be that Ewell fell on his knife."],["Exposing Boo to public attention,","he argues, would be its own kind of cruelty."],["Atticus eventually concedes,","recognizing the compassion behind Tate's reasoning."],["Scout completes the gesture","by walking Boo Radley home herself."],["Standing for a moment on the Radley porch,","she sees the neighborhood as Boo must have seen it."],["The novel closes by suggesting that justice","sometimes means protecting the vulnerable outside the letter of the law."]],
