    gaps:{title:"Concession", bank:["Although Atticus first resists","Even though the law might disagree","While Boo says almost nothing","Despite her earlier fear of him","Much as Jem cannot yet appreciate it","Even if the official account bends the truth"], items:[["___, he eventually accepts Sheriff Tate's reasoning.","Although Atticus first resists"],["___, Sheriff Tate insists that protecting Boo matters more.","Even though the law might disagree"],["___, his presence alone comforts Scout completely.","While Boo says almost nothing"],["___, Scout now walks beside Boo Radley with ease.","Despite her earlier fear of him"],["___, this final act of protection echoes lessons Atticus taught all along.","Much as Jem cannot yet appreciate it"],["___, it succeeds in shielding someone entirely undeserving of public attention.","Even if the official account bends the truth"]]},
